# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded sin(pi x) of BF16
#
# |x| >= 1 that is an integer gives a signed zero, read from the encoding. Otherwise x = x1 + x2, where x1 keeps the
# exponent and the upper 4 bits of the mantissa and x2 the exponent and the lower 3 bits, and sin(pi x) =
# sin(pi x1) cos(pi x2) + cos(pi x1) sin(pi x2), with the four factors B32 values from tables, evaluated with one FMA
# in B32 and rounded once to BF16. Near 0, sin(pi x) rounds like pi x. Round to nearest only.
#
# Also home to the tables cos_pi and tan_pi share: sin and cos of pi x1 and of pi x2.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binaryb16/sinpi/sinpi_bf16.c.
# Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/System/Numerics/BF16

